---
import Arrow from '../../components/Arrow.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import QuoteCta from '../../components/QuoteCta.astro';
import ServiceCard from '../../components/ServiceCard.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { services } from '../../data/services';
import { siteConfig } from '../../data/site';
import { getKeywordTarget, keywordLabel } from '../../lib/seo-keywords';

const seo = getKeywordTarget('/services/');
---

<BaseLayout
  title={keywordLabel(seo.primaryKeyword)}
  description="Compare event, restaurant, wedding, hotel, and healthcare valet parking plus parking management services in Philadelphia and nearby communities."
  canonicalPath="/services/"
  image="/images/event-valet-team.webp"
  imageAlt="Uniformed valet team coordinating vehicle arrivals at a Philadelphia event venue"
  pageType="CollectionPage"
  schema={{
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: siteConfig.url },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Valet parking services', item: `${siteConfig.url}/services/` },
    ],
  }}
>
  <section class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="services-page-title">
    <div class="panel panel-river section-pad">
      <div class="grid-7-6 lg:items-end">
        <div>
          <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Services' }]} />
          <p class="eyebrow mt-6">Service hub</p>
          <h1 id="services-page-title" class="display-title mt-4 max-w-[12ch]">{keywordLabel(seo.primaryKeyword)}.</h1>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="body-large text-ink/70">The work includes one-time event operations, {seo.supportingKeywords[0]}, and {seo.supportingKeywords[1]}. The curb, parking route, timing, and guest handoff determine the operating plan.</p>
          <a href="#service-list" class="button-secondary mt-6">Choose a service<Arrow direction="down" /></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="service-list" class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="service-list-title">
    <div class="panel section-pad">
      <div class="grid-6-7 mb-8 lg:items-end">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Six operating contexts</p>
          <h2 id="service-list-title" class="section-title mt-4">Compare six service types.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="text-lg text-ink/64">Each page explains what changes in that setting, what belongs in the plan, and which details determine staffing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 xl:grid-cols-3">
        {services.map((service, index) => <ServiceCard service={service} index={index} />)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="included-title">
    <div class="panel panel-dark section-pad">
      <div class="grid-5-8">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">What every plan considers</p>
          <h2 id="included-title" class="section-title mt-4">Six inputs shape every parking plan.</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="rule-list border-t border-white/15 p-0" role="list">
          {[
            'Where is the safest, clearest vehicle handoff?',
            'Where can cars be stored, and how long is the retrieval route?',
            'When will arrivals and departures concentrate?',
            'How are keys, tickets, and vehicle locations controlled?',
            'What else uses the curb: pedestrians, deliveries, rideshare, transit, or shuttles?',
            'Who makes the call when conditions change?',
          ].map((text) => (
            <li class="py-5">
              <p class="m-0 text-lg font-semibold text-white/82 sm:text-xl">{text}</p>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="site-frame section-gap" aria-labelledby="service-choice-title">
    <div class="panel section-pad">
      <div class="grid-5-8">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Choosing a service</p>
          <h2 id="service-choice-title" class="section-title mt-4">Some properties need more than one service.</h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-ink/65">A hotel can host a wedding. A restaurant can require recurring dinner coverage and separate event valet. A healthcare or office property may need both guest handoff and broader parking management.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="rich-copy text-lg text-ink/66">
          <p>Start with the movement that creates pressure. If guests arrive within a defined invitation window, the event or wedding pages explain concentrated arrival and departure planning. If vehicles turn over throughout a daily operating period, the restaurant, hotel, and healthcare pages focus on repeatable shifts and communication with the property.</p>
          <p>Parking management applies when the assignment extends beyond taking keys. It may involve lot direction, garage entry, loading coordination, pedestrian separation, overflow, or traffic posts. Valet can be one part of that larger operating plan.</p>
          <p>For a useful first review, share the address, service date or recurring schedule, property type, expected vehicle volume, guest entrance, proposed vehicle-storage area, and the times when arrivals or departures concentrate. Those facts are more useful than selecting a package name before the site is understood.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <QuoteCta eyebrow="Service review" title="Send the property type and operating schedule." body="Include the guest entrance, expected vehicle volume, parking location, and the times when demand concentrates." />
</BaseLayout>
